    "intro_html":  "Kabsa is the national dish of Saudi Arabia and the centerpiece of every family gathering there. Chicken and rice cook in the same pot with a warm spice blend, tomato, and dried lime, then get finished with toasted almonds and golden raisins. Everything happens in one vessel, which is why it feeds a crowd without a sink full of pans. Each bowl carries {{cal}} calories and \u003cstrong\u003e{{protein}} grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e${{cost_ps}} a serving\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
